WHAT YOU MAY DO WITH THIS MOD

Repacking: YES.  Selling: NO.

You may unpack this mod, change it, put it in a modpack, use its models in
your own builds and hand the result to your players. Most DayZ mods forbid that, so
saying nothing would read as a refusal -- this is not one.

Four conditions. The first three are the licence rather than a preference; the
fourth is how PBO signing works:

  1. Say where it came from, and link the Workshop page or the repository.

  2. Keep the same licence on your repack (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), and carry this
     NOTICE with it.

  3. Do not sell it. Running this on a server that takes donations, sells
     cosmetics or sells queue slots is fine -- that is not commercial use.
     Selling the mod itself or any derivative, or putting it behind a paywall
     (a "donate to download" one counts), is not.

  4. Sign your repack with your OWN key, not this one. A key says who stands
     behind a build, and only you can stand behind yours. Generate a pair with
     DSCreateKey.exe from DayZ Tools and ship your own .bikey.


WHERE THE ASSETS COME FROM

Every model and texture here is original work, built for this mod in Blender
from scripts that ship in the repository (models/assets/<radio>/scripts; the
shared pipeline is models/assets/_kit, and the Blender scenes a build saves are
models/assets/<radio>/work/<radio>_high.blend and _game.blend). Public
renders on Sketchfab were used as visual references for proportions and layout
only; no geometry, texture or other data from them is used. The brand on
the cases (OZ-COM), its logo, the model names and all other labels are
invented for the mod and do not reproduce any manufacturer's marks.

